# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The App API — copy to .env and fill in.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# pms_app owns ROWS and nothing else. Connecting as pms_migrate or
# postgres bypasses RLS and makes every isolation guarantee in the
# schema decorative. The health check fails loudly if this is wrong.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://pms_app:CHANGE_ME_app@127.0.0.1:55432/fidato

PORT=8787
NODE_ENV=development
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# The Firebase service account, as one line of JSON. THIS IS A SECRET,
# unlike the web config in src/lib/firebase.ts. Never commit it.
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT={"type":"service_account", ...}

# Development only: the x-dev-staff-id header names the caller, so the
# API can be exercised without a service account. The process REFUSES
# TO START with this set and NODE_ENV=production.
ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=1

# A connection that is NOT subject to row level security, used only by the
# operator tools (preflight, link-staff). They read `hotels` and `staff`
# directly; as `pms_app` with no session set, RLS hands them zero rows and
# every check passes on an empty result. On a deployed box this is the local
# postgres socket:
#
#   ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres@/fidato?host=/var/run/postgresql
#
# The API server itself must NEVER use this.
ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=

# Where uploaded bills are kept. Must NOT be inside the git checkout —
# a deploy that re-clones would take the hotel's invoices with it.
UPLOAD_DIR=

# Optional: n8n copies each bill into Google Drive and posts the link back.
# Nothing breaks when this is unset — the file simply lives only here.
N8N_ATTACHMENT_WEBHOOK=

# ── Sending: the PMS → n8n door (D17-87, D18-20) ────────────────────────
# BOTH must be set or nothing sends at all: no screen offers to send, and no
# row is written. That is the state the system ships in, deliberately — a
# record of what was never attempted is a log of the system's own unfinished
# state, not of anything anybody did.
#
#   N8N_SEND_URL     the workflow's PRODUCTION url from n8n — not the Test
#                    url, which only answers while somebody is watching the
#                    editor. The workflow must be ACTIVE.
#   N8N_SEND_SECRET  the long random text the workflow's first node checks,
#                    sent as `x-fidato-secret`. It is the whole of the
#                    protection on an address that is open to the internet.
#                    ⚠ The OWNER makes it and it lives only here. Never in the
#                      repository, a screen, a test or a chat. It is NOT the
#                      n8n encryption key — that one is a master password and
#                      is never pasted anywhere at all.
#
# The steps that produce both are docs/briefs/n8n-sending.md.
N8N_SEND_URL=
N8N_SEND_SECRET=

# ── The channel manager, SU (D17-66) ────────────────────────────────────
# The owner sets these ON THE SERVER only. They are keys to every booking
# site the group sells on: never in the repository, a screen, a test or a
# chat. Unset, the channel manager simply says it is not set up yet.
#
#   SU_ENVIRONMENT    sandbox (SU's test account) or live
#   SU_CLIENT_ID      from SU when the account is made
#   SU_CLIENT_SECRET  generated on SU's extranet
#   SU_PUSH_KEY       a long random text the OWNER makes, given to SU so it
#                     can push bookings here (D17-79). SU presents it on
#                     every push; anything else is refused with 401.
SU_ENVIRONMENT=
SU_CLIENT_ID=
SU_CLIENT_SECRET=
SU_PUSH_KEY=

# ── The leads app, read only (D27-100, D27-103, D27-170) ─────────────────
# The market-to-revenue app's leads, conversations and ad spend, read LIVE
# when a screen opens; nothing is copied here. Unset, the Leads and WhatsApp
# screen says it is not connected and nothing is read. The steps that make
# the login are src/modules/leads/OWNER-STEPS.md.
#
#   M2R_SERVICE_ACCOUNT  the read-only login's JSON key, ONE LINE, like
#                        FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT. ⚠ A SECRET: the owner puts
#                        it on the server only. Never here, a screen, a test
#                        or a chat. Its one role is Cloud Datastore Viewer.
#   M2R_HOTELS           which PMS hotel is which hotel in the app, e.g.
#                        5EL=five-elements-akkalkot (comma between pairs)
#   M2R_DAILY_READS      the most read in a day, counted from midnight Pacific
#                        (the owner's 5,000, D27-170). The app's free plan is
#                        50,000 a day, SHARED with the app itself.
#   M2R_APP_URL          the app's address, for "Reply in the leads app"
#
#   M2R_EMULATOR         THIS MACHINE ONLY: a stand-in for Google with made-up
#                        leads (the tests, and opening the screens). The server
#                        refuses it under NODE_ENV=production.
M2R_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=
M2R_HOTELS=
M2R_DAILY_READS=
M2R_APP_URL=
